{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a3f7c2e1-4b6d-4e8a-9c2f-xibra-api-batch4",
    "name": "Xibra Platform API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the verified endpoints of **xibra-api** (Batches 1–5): health, authentication, Owner-only invitation management, and public invitation onboarding.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the API: `php artisan serve` inside `D:\\Xibra-Platform\\xibra-api` (default base URL `http://127.0.0.1:8000`).\n2. In this collection's **Variables** tab, set `owner_password` to the value of `XIBRA_OWNER_PASSWORD` from `xibra-api/.env`.\n3. Run the collection in order (Collection Runner) — later requests depend on variables captured by earlier ones:\n   - `POST /auth/login` captures `access_token`\n   - `POST /invitations` captures `invitation_id`, `invitation_code`, `invitation_token`\n   - `POST /invitations/redeem` captures `onboarding_session_token`\n   - `POST /onboarding/complete` captures `onboarding_member_token` and `member_access_token`\n\n## Notes\n\n- The response contract for every endpoint is `{success, message, code, data, meta}` (`docs/api/conventions.md` §5). Clients should branch on `code`, not `message`.\n- A full run **creates one real invitation and revokes it** in the Invitations folder. The Onboarding folder **creates one real Member account and one redeemed invitation**; nothing is deleted. Skip the Onboarding folder if you do not want additional live accounts.\n- The Onboarding complete request derives a unique username and email per run (`member_<timestamp>`), so repeated runs do not collide.\n- Login rate limiting (5/min per identifier, 20/min per IP) and onboarding rate limiting (10/min per IP) are intentionally **not** exercised: triggering them would lock the run for a minute.\n- The member-forbidden check (403) uses the `member_access_token` captured by the Onboarding folder. If that folder is skipped, the variable is empty and the check gracefully falls back to asserting 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.\n- Invitation codes and tokens are returned exactly once, in the create response. The API stores only hashes.\n- All requests send `Content-Type: application/json` and expect JSON responses regardless of the Accept header.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
